  ["joke about snow | snow joke | tell me a joke about snow", "What do you call a snowman in the summer?\nA **puddle**!"],
  ["joke about thunder | thunder joke | tell me a joke about storms", "Why did the lightning bolt get in trouble?\nIt couldn't stop **shocking** everyone!"],
  ["joke about the ocean | funny ocean joke | tell me a joke about the sea", "Why is the ocean always so friendly?\nBecause it likes to **wave** at everyone!"],
  ["funny music joke | another music joke | tell me a music joke please", "Why did the musician bring a ladder to the concert?\nTo reach the **high notes**!"],
  ["joke about a piano | piano joke | tell me a joke about pianos", "Why is a piano so hard to open?\nBecause the **keys** are all on the inside!"],
  ["joke about a guitar | guitar joke | tell me a joke about guitars", "Why did the guitar take a nap?\nBecause it was all **strung** out!"],
  ["joke about a drum | drum joke | tell me a joke about drums", "Why did the drummer get a time-out?\nHe just wouldn't stop **beating** around!"],
  ["joke about singing | singing joke | tell me a joke about singers", "Why did the singer climb the ladder?\nTo reach the **top** of the charts!"],
  ["joke about books | book joke | tell me a joke about books", "Why did the book join the police?\nIt wanted to go undercover... as a **book cover**!"],
  ["joke about reading | reading joke | tell me a joke about reading", "Why was the book so good at baseball?\nIt had a great **story** of hits!"],
  ["joke about writing | pencil joke | tell me a joke about pencils", "Why did the pencil feel pointless?\nIt just needed a little **sharpening** up!"],
  ["funny school joke | another school joke | tell me a school joke please", "Why did the broom get a bad grade?\nIt kept **sweeping** through its homework!"],
  ["joke about a teacher | funny teacher joke | tell me a joke about teachers", "Why did the teacher wear sunglasses to class?\nBecause her students were so **bright**!"],
  ["joke about geography | geography joke | tell me a joke about maps", "Why is the map always so calm?\nBecause it knows all the right **directions**!"],
  ["joke about history | history joke | tell me a joke about history", "Why did the history book look so tired?\nBecause it had so many **dates**!"],
  ["joke about sports | another sports joke | tell me a sports joke please", "Why did the basketball player bring string to the game?\nSo he could **tie** the score!"],
  ["joke about soccer | another soccer joke | tell me a soccer joke please", "Why did the soccer field get bigger?\nBecause the players kept **stretching** it with corner kicks... just kidding, they just wanted more room to run!"],
  ["joke about swimming | swimming joke | tell me a joke about swimming", "Why don't swimmers tell secrets by the pool?\nBecause they're afraid of a little **leak**!"],
  ["joke about baseball | baseball joke | tell me a joke about baseball", "Why was Cinderella bad at baseball?\nShe had a pumpkin for a coach and kept **running** away from the ball!"],
  ["joke about a bicycle | bicycle joke | tell me a joke about bikes", "Why couldn't the bicycle stand up by itself?\nBecause it was **two-tired**!"],
  ["joke about a car | car joke | tell me a joke about cars", "Why did the car get a flat tire?\nBecause there was a **fork** in the road!"],
  ["joke about a train | train joke | tell me a joke about trains", "What do you call a train that sneezes?\nAchoo-choo train!"],
  ["joke about an airplane | airplane joke | tell me a joke about planes", "Why don't airplanes ever get tired?\nBecause they always have plenty of **wing**-power!"],
  ["joke about a boat | boat joke | tell me a joke about boats", "What did the sea say to the boat?\nNothing, it just gave a little **wave**!"],
  ["pun about time | time pun | give me a pun about clocks", "I was going to tell you a pun about a broken clock, but it's about **time** I stopped!"],
  ["pun about vegetables | vegetable pun | give me a pun about veggies", "I'm rooting for you! You're the best thing since **sliced** carrots, and I'm not just saying that from the bottom of my **beet**!"],
  ["pun about reading | book pun | give me a pun about books", "I couldn't put my book about gravity down. It was **impossible to put down** because it really pulled me in!"],
  ["pun about electricity | electric pun | give me a pun about electricity", "I told an electricity pun, but it didn't get a great re-**volt**. Still, the response was pretty **shocking**!"],
  ["pun about the ocean | ocean pun | give me a pun about the sea", "What did the beach say when the tide came in?\n\"Long time, no **sea**!\""],
  ["pun about plants | plant pun | give me a pun about plants", "I wanted to tell you a plant pun, but I was afraid it would never **grow** on you. Thanks for **sticking** around anyway!"],
  ["pun about music notes | music pun | give me a pun about music", "I wrote a song about a tortilla. Well, actually it's more of a **wrap**!"],
  ["pun about the weather | weather pun | give me a pun about the weather", "Thunder and lightning were having a race. The lightning won, but the thunder made a **big noise** about coming second!"],
  ["pun about math | math pun | give me a pun about numbers", "Why was the equals sign so humble?\nBecause it knew it wasn't **greater than** or **less than** anyone else!"],
  ["pun about sleep | sleep pun | give me a pun about being tired", "I used to be a baker, but I couldn't make enough **dough**, and it left me totally **crumb**-pletely exhausted!"],
  ["knock knock joke about a cow | cow knock knock joke | a new knock knock joke", "Knock knock.\nWho's there?\nCow says.\nCow says who?\nNo, silly, a cow says **moo**!"],
  ["knock knock joke about an orange | orange knock knock joke | knock knock orange", "Knock knock.\nWho's there?\nOrange.\nOrange who?\nOrange you glad I came to say hello?"],
  ["knock knock joke about a banana | banana knock knock joke | knock knock banana", "Knock knock.\nWho's there?\nBanana.\nBanana who?\nKnock knock. Who's there? Banana. Banana who? Knock knock. Who's there? Orange. Orange who? Orange you glad I didn't say banana again?"],
  ["knock knock joke about the weather | knock knock about the sun | sunny knock knock joke", "Knock knock.\nWho's there?\nHoney bee.\nHoney bee who?\nHoney bee a dear and let me in, it's sunny out here!"],
  ["knock knock joke about a duck | duck knock knock joke | knock knock duck", "Knock knock.\nWho's there?\nA little old lady.\nA little old lady who?\nI didn't know you could **yodel**!"],
  ["fun fact about sloths | sloth fun fact | tell me a fun fact about sloths", "Fun fact: Sloths are so slow that algae can grow on their fur, giving them a slightly green tint that helps them hide in the trees!"],
  ["fun fact about giraffes | giraffe fun fact | tell me a fun fact about giraffes", "Fun fact: A giraffe's tongue can be about 45 to 50 cm (18 to 20 inches) long, and it's dark purple-blue, which may help protect it from sunburn while it eats!"],
  ["fun fact about flamingos | flamingo fun fact | tell me a fun fact about flamingos", "Fun fact: Flamingos aren't born pink! They turn pink over time from the tiny shrimp and algae they eat."],
  ["fun fact about jellyfish | jellyfish fun fact | tell me a fun fact about jellyfish", "Fun fact: Jellyfish have no brain, no heart and no bones, and they've been drifting through the oceans for over 500 million years, long before the dinosaurs!"],
  ["fun fact about starfish | starfish fun fact | tell me a fun fact about starfish", "Fun fact: Starfish don't have a brain or blood, and many can regrow a whole arm if they lose one. Scientists often call them 'sea stars' because they aren't really fish!"],
  ["fun fact about seahorses | seahorse fun fact | tell me a fun fact about seahorses", "Fun fact: In seahorses, it's the dad who gets pregnant! The father carries the eggs in a special pouch and gives birth to the babies."],
  ["fun fact about dolphins | dolphin fun fact | tell me a fun fact about dolphins", "Fun fact: Dolphins sleep with only half their brain at a time, so one eye stays open. That way they can keep breathing and watch for danger even while resting!"],
  ["fun fact about elephants | elephant fun fact | tell me a fun fact about elephants", "Fun fact: Elephants are the only animals that can't jump, but they can swim very well and even use their trunks like a snorkel!"],
  ["fun fact about koalas | koala fun fact | tell me a fun fact about koalas", "Fun fact: Koalas have fingerprints so similar to human ones that they could confuse a crime scene! They're one of the few animals with ridged prints like ours."],
  ["fun fact about octopuses | octopus fun fact | tell me a fun fact about octopuses", "Fun fact: An octopus can taste with its arms! Each sucker has sensors, so it can feel and taste whatever it touches."],
  ["fun fact about honeybees | bee fun fact | tell me a fun fact about bees", "Fun fact: A honeybee has to visit around two million flowers to make just one pound (about half a kilogram) of honey!"],
  ["fun fact about ants | ant fun fact | tell me a fun fact about ants", "Fun fact: Ants never sleep the way we do, and together all the ants on Earth may weigh about as much as all the humans combined!"],
  ["fun fact about butterflies | butterfly fun fact | tell me a fun fact about butterflies", "Fun fact: Butterflies taste with their feet! They stand on a leaf or flower to find out whether it's good to eat or a good spot to lay eggs."],
  ["fun fact about spiders | spider fun fact | tell me a fun fact about spiders", "Fun fact: Some spider silk is, pound for pound, stronger than steel. If you could make a strand as thick as a pencil, it could be tough enough to stop a jet!"],
  ["fun fact about frogs | frog fun fact | tell me a fun fact about frogs", "Fun fact: Many frogs use their eyeballs to help swallow! They pull their eyes down into their heads to push food down their throats."],
  ["fun fact about snails | snail fun fact | tell me a fun fact about snails", "Fun fact: A snail can sleep for up to three years if the weather is too dry or cold, tucking itself safely inside its shell until conditions improve."],
  ["fun fact about owls | owl fun fact | tell me a fun fact about owls", "Fun fact: An owl can turn its head about 270 degrees! Its eyes can't move in their sockets, so it spins its head to look around instead."],
  ["fun fact about penguins | penguin fun fact | tell me a fun fact about penguins", "Fun fact: Emperor penguin dads balance the egg on their feet and go about two months without eating while they keep it warm through the Antarctic winter!"],
  ["fun fact about polar bears | polar bear fun fact | tell me a fun fact about polar bears", "Fun fact: Polar bears have black skin under their fur, which helps them soak up the sun's warmth, and their fur is actually see-through, not white!"],
  ["fun fact about pandas | panda fun fact | tell me a fun fact about pandas", "Fun fact: A newborn giant panda is about the size of a stick of butter, roughly 900 times smaller than its mother!"],
  ["fun fact about cheetahs | cheetah fun fact | tell me a fun fact about cheetahs", "Fun fact: A cheetah can go from standing still to about 100 km/h (60 mph) in just three seconds, which is faster than most sports cars!"],
  ["fun fact about hummingbirds | hummingbird fun fact | tell me a fun fact about hummingbirds", "Fun fact: Hummingbirds are the only birds that can fly backwards, and their wings can beat about 50 times per second!"],
  ["fun fact about your body | human body fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the body", "Fun fact: Your body makes a brand new layer of skin about every month, and over a lifetime you shed enough skin to fill several large bags!"],
  ["fun fact about the brain | brain fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the brain", "Fun fact: Your brain uses about 20 percent of your body's energy even though it only weighs around 2 percent of your body, and it never truly 'turns off'!"],
  ["fun fact about the heart | heart fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the heart", "Fun fact: Your heart beats about 100,000 times a day, and over an average lifetime that's more than two and a half billion beats!"],
  ["fun fact about bones | bone fun fact | tell me a fun fact about bones", "Fun fact: Your bones are, gram for gram, stronger than steel in some ways, and the hard outer part of a bone could support a lot of weight before it breaks!"],
  ["fun fact about blood | blood fun fact | tell me a fun fact about blood", "Fun fact: Your body has about 100,000 km (60,000 miles) of blood vessels, enough to wrap around the Earth more than twice if you lined them up!"],
  ["fun fact about the tongue | tongue fun fact | tell me a fun fact about taste", "Fun fact: Your tongue print is as unique as your fingerprint, and your taste buds are replaced every week or two!"],
  ["fun fact about sneezing | sneeze fun fact | tell me a fun fact about sneezing", "Fun fact: A sneeze can shoot out of your nose and mouth at around 160 km/h (100 mph), which is why you should always cover it!"],
  ["fun fact about the eyes | eye fun fact | tell me a fun fact about eyes", "Fun fact: Your eyes blink around 15 to 20 times a minute, which adds up to roughly 10 million blinks in a year!"],
  ["cool fun fact about space | another space fun fact | tell me a fun fact about outer space", "Fun fact: There are more stars in the universe than grains of sand on all the beaches on Earth, and that's a number far too big to really imagine!"],
  ["fun fact about the sun | sun fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the sun", "Fun fact: The Sun is so big that about 1.3 million Earths could fit inside it, and it makes up more than 99 percent of all the mass in our solar system!"],
  ["fun fact about the moon | moon fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the moon", "Fun fact: The footprints the astronauts left on the Moon could stay there for millions of years, because there's no wind or rain to wipe them away!"],
  ["fun fact about mars | mars fun fact | tell me a fun fact about mars", "Fun fact: Mars is home to the tallest volcano in the solar system, Olympus Mons, which is about three times taller than Mount Everest!"],
  ["fun fact about jupiter | jupiter fun fact | tell me a fun fact about jupiter", "Fun fact: Jupiter is so huge that all the other planets in our solar system could fit inside it, and its Great Red Spot is a storm bigger than Earth!"],
  ["fun fact about saturn | saturn fun fact | tell me a fun fact about saturn", "Fun fact: Saturn is so light for its size that if you could find a bathtub big enough, the whole planet would float in the water!"],
  ["fun fact about venus | venus fun fact | tell me a fun fact about venus", "Fun fact: A day on Venus is longer than its year! It spins so slowly that one Venus day lasts longer than the time it takes to orbit the Sun."],
  ["fun fact about a black hole | black hole fun fact | tell me a fun fact about black holes", "Fun fact: A black hole's gravity is so strong that not even light can escape it, which is exactly why it looks black and invisible!"],
  ["fun fact about the milky way | galaxy fun fact | tell me a fun fact about our galaxy", "Fun fact: Our Milky Way galaxy has somewhere between 100 and 400 billion stars, and our Sun is just one ordinary star near the edge of it!"],
  ["fun fact about shooting stars | shooting star fun fact | tell me a fun fact about meteors", "Fun fact: A 'shooting star' isn't a star at all. It's a tiny bit of space rock, often no bigger than a grain of sand, burning up as it enters our atmosphere!"],
  ["fun fact about the deep ocean | another ocean fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the ocean", "Fun fact: We've explored only about 5 percent of the ocean, so there are mountains, valleys and creatures down there that no human has ever seen!"],
  ["fun fact about water | water fun fact | tell me a fun fact about water", "Fun fact: The water you drank today may have once been sipped by a dinosaur! Water keeps cycling through the planet over and over for millions of years."],
  ["fun fact about lightning | lightning fun fact | tell me a fun fact about lightning", "Fun fact: A bolt of lightning is about five times hotter than the surface of the Sun, which is why it heats the air so fast it makes thunder!"],
  ["fun fact about rainbows | rainbow fun fact | tell me a fun fact about rainbows", "Fun fact: No two people ever see exactly the same rainbow, because the one you see depends on exactly where your own eyes are standing!"],
  ["fun fact about clouds | cloud fun fact | tell me a fun fact about clouds", "Fun fact: A fluffy white cloud can weigh around a million pounds (about 500,000 kg), as much as 100 elephants, but it floats because it's spread over a huge space!"],
  ["fun fact about snowflakes | snowflake fun fact | tell me a fun fact about snow", "Fun fact: Every snowflake has six sides, and because of the way they form, it's almost certain no two snowflakes are ever exactly alike!"],
  ["fun fact about volcanoes | volcano fun fact | tell me a fun fact about volcanoes", "Fun fact: There are around 1,500 volcanoes on land that could still erupt, plus thousands more hidden under the ocean that we rarely get to see!"],
  ["fun fact about earthquakes | earthquake fun fact | tell me a fun fact about earthquakes", "Fun fact: Tiny earthquakes happen all over the world every single day, far more than we feel, often thousands in a year that are too small to notice!"],
  ["fun fact about mountains | mountain fun fact | tell me a fun fact about mountains", "Fun fact: Mount Everest grows a few millimetres taller almost every year, because the plates of the Earth are still slowly pushing it up!"],
  ["fun fact about the sahara desert | desert fun fact | tell me a fun fact about deserts", "Fun fact: The Sahara Desert is almost as big as the whole United States, and even though it's famous for heat, it can get cold enough to snow in places at night!"],
  ["fun fact about trees | tree fun fact | tell me a fun fact about trees", "Fun fact: Some trees can 'talk' to each other through a huge underground network of fungi, sharing food and even warnings about insects!"],
  ["fun fact about plants | plant fun fact | tell me a fun fact about plants", "Fun fact: Plants make the oxygen we breathe using sunlight, water and air through a process called photosynthesis, so in a way trees are helping you breathe right now!"],
  ["fun fact about bananas | banana fun fact | tell me a fun fact about bananas", "Fun fact: Bananas are berries, but strawberries are not! In botany, the way the fruit grows is what decides, and bananas tick the 'berry' boxes."],
  ["fun fact about honey | honey fun fact | tell me a fun fact about honey", "Fun fact: Honey never spoils if it's sealed well. Archaeologists have found pots of honey in ancient tombs that were thousands of years old and still safe to eat!"],
  ["fun fact about chocolate | chocolate fun fact | tell me a fun fact about chocolate", "Fun fact: Chocolate comes from the seeds of the cacao tree, and people have enjoyed it for over 3,000 years, once even using the beans as money!"],
  ["fun fact about popcorn | popcorn fun fact | tell me a fun fact about popcorn", "Fun fact: Popcorn pops because each kernel holds a tiny drop of water inside, and when it heats up the water turns to steam and bursts the kernel open!"],
  ["fun fact about ice cream | ice cream fun fact | tell me a fun fact about ice cream", "Fun fact: It takes about 50 licks to finish a single scoop of ice cream, so your tongue gets a fun little workout every time!"],
  ["fun fact about eggs | egg fun fact | tell me a fun fact about eggs", "Fun fact: You can tell if an egg is fresh by putting it in water: a fresh egg sinks and lays flat, while an old one floats because of the air inside!"],
  ["fun fact about pineapples | pineapple fun fact | tell me a fun fact about pineapples", "Fun fact: A pineapple isn't a single fruit. It's actually made of dozens of tiny fruits fused together, and it can take almost two years to grow one!"],
  ["fun fact about the eiffel tower | eiffel tower fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the eiffel tower", "Fun fact: The Eiffel Tower can grow about 15 cm (6 inches) taller in summer, because the metal expands in the heat and shrinks back when it's cold!"],
  ["fun fact about the great wall of china | great wall fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the great wall", "Fun fact: The Great Wall of China is thousands of kilometres long, but despite the popular myth, you cannot actually see it from the Moon with the naked eye!"],
  ["fun fact about the pyramids | pyramid fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the pyramids", "Fun fact: The Great Pyramid of Giza was the tallest building made by humans for about 3,800 years, until cathedrals finally grew taller in the Middle Ages!"],
  ["fun fact about the statue of liberty | statue of liberty fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the statue of liberty", "Fun fact: The Statue of Liberty was a gift from France, and her green color comes from the copper on the outside slowly reacting with the air over time!"],
  ["fun fact about airplanes | airplane fun fact | tell me a fun fact about planes", "Fun fact: The food on airplanes can taste different because the dry cabin air and the noise actually dull your sense of taste, especially for salty and sweet flavors!"],
  ["fun fact about the first computer | computer fun fact | tell me a fun fact about computers", "Fun fact: One of the first general computers, ENIAC, filled a whole room and weighed about 30 tons, yet a modern phone is millions of times faster than it!"],
  ["fun fact about the internet | internet fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the internet", "Fun fact: The very first message ever sent over the early internet in 1969 was meant to be 'LOGIN', but the system crashed after just two letters: 'LO'!"],
  ["fun fact about emoji | emoji fun fact | tell me a fun fact about emojis", "Fun fact: The most popular emoji in the world is usually the 'face with tears of joy', and there are now thousands of emojis to choose from!"],
  ["fun fact about video games | video game fun fact | tell me a fun fact about video games", "Fun fact: The famous jumping character Mario was first called 'Jumpman', and he started out as a carpenter before becoming a plumber!"],
  ["fun fact about numbers | number fun fact | tell me a fun fact about math", "Fun fact: Zero is the only number that can't be written in Roman numerals, because the ancient Romans simply had no symbol for 'nothing'!"],
  ["fun fact about pi | pi fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the number pi", "Fun fact: The number pi goes on forever without repeating, and computers have calculated it to trillions of digits, but it never settles into a pattern!"],
  ["fun fact about the color blue | color fun fact | tell me a fun fact about colors", "Fun fact: True blue is one of the rarest colors in nature, which is why blue animals and flowers often look blue through clever tricks of light rather than blue pigment!"],
  ["fun fact about dreams | dream fun fact | tell me a fun fact about dreaming", "Fun fact: You forget about half of a dream within five minutes of waking up, and almost all of it within ten, which is why dreams can feel so slippery!"],
  ["fun fact about laughing | laughter fun fact | tell me a fun fact about laughing", "Fun fact: You almost can't tickle yourself, because your brain knows it's coming and cancels the surprise that makes tickling feel ticklish!"],
  ["fun fact about yawning | yawn fun fact | tell me a fun fact about yawning", "Fun fact: Yawns really are contagious: just seeing, hearing, or even reading about a yawn can make you want to do one. Did you yawn just now?"],
  ["fun fact about goosebumps | goosebumps fun fact | tell me a fun fact about goosebumps", "Fun fact: Goosebumps are left over from our furry ancestors! Tiny muscles pull your hairs up to trap warmth or look bigger, even though we're not very hairy anymore."],
  ["fun fact about hiccups | hiccup fun fact | tell me a fun fact about hiccups", "Fun fact: Hiccups happen when a big muscle under your lungs, the diaphragm, twitches suddenly, and the funny 'hic' sound comes from your vocal cords snapping shut!"],
  ["fun fact about sleep | sleep fun fact | tell me a fun fact about sleep", "Fun fact: You spend about a third of your whole life asleep, which for many people adds up to around 25 years of sleeping over a lifetime!"],
  ["fun fact about the great barrier reef | coral reef fun fact | tell me a fun fact about coral reefs", "Fun fact: The Great Barrier Reef is the largest living structure on Earth, so big it can be seen from space, and it's made by tiny animals called coral polyps!"],
  ["fun fact about kangaroos | kangaroo fun fact | tell me a fun fact about kangaroos", "Fun fact: Kangaroos can't walk backwards easily, which is one reason a kangaroo appears on Australia's coat of arms: a symbol of always moving forward!"],
  ["fun fact about crocodiles | crocodile fun fact | tell me a fun fact about crocodiles", "Fun fact: A crocodile can't stick out its tongue, because it's attached to the roof of its mouth, and it has one of the strongest bites of any animal on Earth!"],
  ["fun fact about tigers | tiger fun fact | tell me a fun fact about tigers", "Fun fact: A tiger's stripes are like a fingerprint, no two are the same, and the stripes grow on their skin too, not just their fur!"],
  ["fun fact about wolves | wolf fun fact | tell me a fun fact about wolves", "Fun fact: A wolf's howl can be heard up to about 10 km (6 miles) away in the right conditions, and packs use howling to find each other and stay together!"],
  ["fun fact about bats | bat fun fact | tell me a fun fact about bats", "Fun fact: Bats are the only mammals that can truly fly, and some tiny bats can eat over 1,000 mosquitoes in a single hour!"],
  ["fun fact about chameleons | chameleon fun fact | tell me a fun fact about chameleons", "Fun fact: A chameleon can move its two eyes in different directions at the same time, so it can watch for food with one eye and danger with the other!"],
  ["fun fact about pigeons | pigeon fun fact | tell me a fun fact about pigeons", "Fun fact: Pigeons can find their way home from hundreds of kilometres away, and long ago they carried important messages during wars and emergencies!"],
  ["fun fact about crows | crow fun fact | tell me a fun fact about crows", "Fun fact: Crows are so clever they can recognise human faces, use tools, and even hold a grudge against a person who was mean to them!"],
  ["fun fact about rats | rat fun fact | tell me a fun fact about rats", "Fun fact: Rats are ticklish and will 'laugh' with tiny high-pitched squeaks, far too high for us to hear, when they're gently tickled and happy!"],
  ["fun fact about tardigrades | water bear fun fact | tell me a fun fact about tardigrades", "Fun fact: Tiny creatures called tardigrades, or 'water bears', are so tough they can survive being frozen, boiled, dried out, and even a trip into outer space!"],
  ["fun fact about cats | cat fun fact | tell me a fun fact about cats", "Fun fact: A cat's purr vibrates at a frequency that may help heal bones and muscles, so purring might actually be a little self-repair system!"],
  ["fun fact about dogs | dog fun fact | tell me a fun fact about dogs", "Fun fact: A dog's sense of smell is tens of thousands of times stronger than ours, and each dog's nose print is as unique as a human fingerprint!"],
  ["fun fact about horses | horse fun fact | tell me a fun fact about horses", "Fun fact: Horses can sleep both standing up and lying down, and they can even nap on their feet thanks to a special locking system in their legs!"],
  ["fun fact about the color of the sky | sky fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the sky", "Fun fact: The sky looks blue because tiny bits of air scatter the blue light from the Sun in all directions more than the other colors!"],
  ["fun fact about salt | salt fun fact | tell me a fun fact about salt", "Fun fact: Salt was once so valuable that Roman soldiers were sometimes paid in it, and that's where the word 'salary' comes from!"],
  ["fun fact about the olympics | olympics fun fact | tell me a fun fact about the olympics", "Fun fact: The ancient Olympic Games began in Greece over 2,700 years ago, and the five Olympic rings stand for the five inhabited areas of the world coming together!"],
  ["how many sides are on a hexagon | sides on a hexagon | hexagon sides", "A hexagon has **6 sides** (and 6 corners). 'Hexa' is a Greek word for six."],
  ["how many sides are on a pentagon | sides on a pentagon | pentagon sides", "A pentagon has **5 sides**. 'Penta' means five, so a pentagon is a five-sided shape."],
  ["how many sides are on an octagon | sides on an octagon | octagon sides", "An octagon has **8 sides**. A classic example is a stop sign, which is shaped like an octagon!"],
  ["how many sides does a triangle have | sides on a triangle | triangle sides", "A triangle has **3 sides** and 3 corners, and its three angles always add up to 180 degrees."],
  ["what is the hardest natural substance on earth | hardest natural material | what is the hardest thing in nature", "The hardest known natural substance is **diamond**. It's made of carbon atoms arranged in a very strong, tightly bonded structure."],
  ["what is the tallest mountain on the planet | highest mountain on earth | tallest mountain", "**Mount Everest** is the tallest mountain above sea level, at about 8,849 m (29,032 ft), on the border of Nepal and Tibet."],
  ["what is the longest river on earth | the single longest river | biggest river", "The **Nile** and the **Amazon** are the two longest rivers, each over 6,500 km (about 4,000 miles). Scientists still debate which one is truly longest!"],
  ["what is the biggest ocean in the world | the biggest ocean of all | largest ocean on earth", "The **Pacific Ocean** is the largest and deepest ocean, covering about a third of the Earth's surface, bigger than all the land on the planet combined."],
  ["what is the biggest desert on earth | the biggest desert of all | largest desert", "The largest desert is actually **Antarctica**! A desert is any place that gets very little rain or snow, and the frozen continent is the biggest of all."],
  ["what is the smallest planet in the solar system | smallest planet | tiniest planet", "**Mercury** is the smallest planet in our solar system, and it's also the closest one to the Sun."],
  ["what is the largest planet in the solar system | biggest planet | largest planet", "**Jupiter** is the largest planet in our solar system, so big that more than 1,300 Earths could fit inside it."],
  ["how many continents are there in the world | total number of continents | how many continents on earth", "There are **7 continents**: Africa, Antarctica, Asia, Australia (Oceania), Europe, North America and South America."],
  ["how many oceans are there on earth | total number of oceans | how many oceans on earth", "There are **5 oceans**: the Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Southern (Antarctic) and Arctic."],
  ["how many colors are in a rainbow | colors of the rainbow | how many colours in a rainbow", "A rainbow has **7 colors**: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet. A handy name to remember them is 'Roy G. Biv'!"],
  ["how many days are in a leap year | days in a leap year | leap year days", "A leap year has **366 days**, one more than usual. The extra day, February 29, is added about every four years to keep our calendar in step with the seasons."],
  ["how many days are in a year | days in a year | number of days in a year", "A normal year has **365 days**. It actually takes the Earth about 365 and a quarter days to orbit the Sun, which is why we add a leap day every four years."],
  ["how many hours are in a day | hours in a day | number of hours in a day", "There are **24 hours** in a day, which is roughly how long it takes the Earth to spin around once on its axis."],
  ["how many minutes are in an hour | minutes in an hour | number of minutes in an hour", "There are **60 minutes** in an hour, and 60 seconds in each minute, so an hour has 3,600 seconds."],
  ["how many seconds are in a minute | seconds in a minute | number of seconds in a minute", "There are **60 seconds** in a minute. This way of counting time in sixties comes from the ancient Babylonians thousands of years ago."],
  ["how many weeks are in a year | weeks in a calendar year | number of weeks in a year", "There are **52 weeks** in a year (with one or two extra days left over, which is why the same date lands on a different weekday each year)."],
  ["how many months have 31 days | months with 31 days | which months have 31 days", "**Seven months** have 31 days: January, March, May, July, August, October and December. A knuckle trick can help you remember them!"],
  ["what is the largest animal on earth | biggest animal | largest animal ever", "The **blue whale** is the largest animal ever known to have lived, even bigger than the dinosaurs, reaching about 30 m (nearly 100 ft) long."],
  ["which is the fastest land animal | fastest land running animal | quickest land animal", "The **cheetah** is the fastest land animal, able to sprint at around 100 to 120 km/h (60 to 75 mph) for short bursts."],
  ["what is the tallest animal in the world | tallest animal | tallest land animal", "The **giraffe** is the tallest animal on Earth, with adults standing around 5 to 6 m (16 to 19 ft) tall."],
  ["what is the slowest animal in the world | slowest animal | slowest land animal", "The **three-toed sloth** is one of the slowest animals, moving so slowly that it may travel only a few metres in a whole minute."],
  ["what is the smallest bird in the world | smallest bird | tiniest bird", "The **bee hummingbird** is the smallest bird in the world, barely bigger than a bee, measuring only about 5 to 6 cm long."],
  ["how many teeth does an adult human have | adult teeth | number of teeth in an adult", "A full set of adult teeth is **32 teeth**, including the wisdom teeth. Children have 20 baby teeth, which fall out to make room for the adult ones."],
  ["how many bones is a baby born with | baby bones | number of bones in a baby", "A baby is born with around **270 bones**. As a child grows, some of these bones fuse together, leaving about 206 in an adult."],
  ["what is the chemical symbol for water | formula for water | water chemical formula", "The chemical formula for water is **H2O**: two hydrogen atoms joined to one oxygen atom in each tiny water molecule."],
  ["what is the symbol for gold on the periodic table | symbol for gold | gold chemical symbol", "The chemical symbol for gold is **Au**, from its old Latin name 'aurum', which means 'shining dawn'."],
  ["what is the chemical symbol for oxygen | chemical sign for oxygen | oxygen chemical symbol", "The chemical symbol for oxygen is **O**. The air we breathe is about 21 percent oxygen, and our bodies need it to make energy."],
  ["what is the biggest country on earth | the biggest country of all | largest country by area", "**Russia** is the largest country in the world by area, so big it stretches across 11 time zones from Europe into Asia."],
  ["what is the tiniest country on earth | the smallest country of all | the tiniest country of all", "**Vatican City** is the smallest country in the world, a tiny city-state inside Rome, Italy, that you could walk across in a few minutes."],
  ["what language is spoken most in the world | most spoken language | which language has the most total speakers", "When you count everyone who speaks it, **English** has the most total speakers, while **Mandarin Chinese** has the most native speakers."],
  ["what planet is known as the red planet | which planet is the red planet | red planet name", "**Mars** is known as the Red Planet. Its reddish color comes from iron in its soil that has rusted, a bit like rusty metal here on Earth."],
  ["what is the closest planet to the sun | closest planet to the sun | nearest planet to the sun", "**Mercury** is the closest planet to the Sun. Even so, it's not the hottest planet; Venus is, because of its thick, heat-trapping clouds."],
  ["what is the hottest planet in the solar system | hottest planet | what planet is the hottest one", "**Venus** is the hottest planet, with surface temperatures around 465 degrees C (870 degrees F), because its thick atmosphere traps heat like a blanket."],
  ["how many legs does a butterfly have | butterfly legs | number of legs on a butterfly", "A butterfly has **6 legs**, like all insects, even though they can be hard to spot because the front pair is sometimes small and tucked up."],
  ["how many hearts does an earthworm have | earthworm hearts | number of hearts in a worm", "An earthworm has **five pairs of heart-like structures** (often counted as 10) that pump its blood, though they're simpler than a human heart."],
  ["what is the largest organ in the human body | biggest organ | largest organ of the body", "Your **skin** is the largest organ of your body! It protects you, keeps water in, and helps control your temperature."],
  ["what is the strongest muscle in the human body | the body's strongest muscle | which muscle is the strongest", "For its size, the **masseter** (your jaw muscle) is one of the strongest, giving you a powerful bite. The heart and the muscles in your tongue are impressively strong too!"],
  ["what is the fastest fish in the ocean | fastest fish | quickest fish", "The **sailfish** is often called the fastest fish, able to swim in short bursts of around 110 km/h (68 mph)."],
  ["what is the deepest point of the sea | deepest point in the ocean | deepest place in the sea", "The deepest known point is the **Mariana Trench** in the Pacific Ocean, reaching about 11 km (nearly 7 miles) down, deeper than Everest is tall."],
  ["how long does it take the earth to orbit the sun | earth orbit time | how long is earth's orbit around the sun", "It takes the Earth about **365 and a quarter days** (one year) to travel all the way around the Sun."],
  ["how long does it take the moon to orbit the earth | moon orbit time | how long is the moon's orbit", "The Moon takes about **27 days** to orbit the Earth, and roughly 29.5 days to go through a full cycle of phases from one new moon to the next."],
  ["how far is the sun from the earth | distance to the sun | how far away is the sun", "The Sun is about **150 million km (93 million miles)** from Earth. Light from the Sun takes a little over eight minutes to reach us!"],
  ["how fast is the speed of light in a vacuum | how fast does light move | speed of light", "Light travels at about **300,000 km per second (186,000 miles per second)**, fast enough to circle the whole Earth more than seven times in one second!"],
  ["what gas do plants take in | what do plants breathe in | gas plants use from the air", "Plants take in **carbon dioxide** from the air and, using sunlight and water, turn it into food and release oxygen in a process called photosynthesis."],
  ["what gas do humans breathe in to survive | what do we breathe in | gas humans need to breathe", "Humans breathe in **oxygen** to survive, and breathe out carbon dioxide. Your lungs pass oxygen into your blood so it can travel to the rest of your body."],
  ["how many strings does a standard violin have | violin strings | number of strings on a violin", "A standard violin has **4 strings**, tuned to the notes G, D, A and E from lowest to highest."],
  ["how many players are on a baseball team on the field | baseball players on the field | number of players in baseball", "Each baseball team has **9 players** on the field at a time, including the pitcher and the catcher."],
  ["how many squares are on a chessboard | squares on a chess board | number of squares on a chessboard", "A chessboard has **64 squares** in an 8-by-8 grid, in alternating light and dark colors."],
  ["how many points is a touchdown worth in american football | touchdown points | value of a touchdown", "A touchdown in American football is worth **6 points**, and the team can then try for 1 or 2 more points right after it."],
  ["how many degrees are in a circle | degrees in a circle | total degrees of a circle", "A full circle has **360 degrees**. Half a circle is 180 degrees, and a right angle (a square corner) is 90 degrees."],
  ["how many degrees are in a right angle | degrees in a right angle | right angle degrees", "A right angle has **90 degrees**. It's the square corner you see in a book, a window or the letter L."],
  ["what is the freezing point of water in celsius | freezing point of water | what temperature does water freeze at", "Water freezes at **0 degrees Celsius** (32 degrees Fahrenheit) at normal pressure, turning from liquid into solid ice."],
  ["what is the boiling point of water in celsius | boiling point of water | what temperature does water boil at", "Water boils at **100 degrees Celsius** (212 degrees Fahrenheit) at sea level, turning from liquid into steam."],
  ["how many letters are in the english alphabet | letters in the alphabet | number of letters in the alphabet", "The English alphabet has **26 letters**: 5 vowels (a, e, i, o, u) and 21 consonants, with 'y' sometimes acting as a vowel too."],
  ["how many planets have rings | which planets in our solar system have rings | planets with rings", "**Four planets** have rings: Saturn, Jupiter, Uranus and Neptune. Saturn's rings are by far the biggest and brightest."],
  ["what is the largest mammal on land | biggest land mammal | biggest land animal on earth", "The **African elephant** is the largest land mammal, with big males weighing as much as 6,000 kg (around 13,000 pounds)."],
  ["how many colors are on a traffic light | traffic light colors | colors of a traffic light", "A traffic light has **3 colors**: red means stop, yellow (amber) means slow down and get ready, and green means go."],
  ["how many wheels does a standard car have | wheels on a car | number of wheels on a car", "A standard car has **4 wheels**. Most also carry a spare wheel in case one gets a flat tire."],
  ["how many legs does a crab have | crab legs | number of legs on a crab", "A crab has **10 legs** in total, including its two front claws (called pincers), which it uses to grab food and defend itself."],
  ["how many eyes does a bee have | bee eyes | number of eyes on a bee", "A honeybee has **5 eyes**: two big compound eyes on the sides of its head and three tiny simple eyes on top that help it sense light."],
  ["what is the tallest tree in the world | tallest tree | biggest tree", "The tallest trees are the **coast redwoods** of California, which can grow over 100 m (around 350 ft) tall, as high as a 30-story building!"],
  ["how many strings on a standard harp | harp strings | number of strings on a harp", "A modern concert harp usually has around **47 strings**, and the player plucks them with both hands to make its gentle, flowing sound."],
  ["what is the most common blood type | most common blood type | which blood type is most common", "Worldwide, **O positive** is generally the most common blood type, though exact amounts vary from place to place."],
  ["how many teeth does a great white shark have | great white shark teeth | shark teeth count", "A great white shark can have about **300 teeth** at once, arranged in several rows, and it grows new ones throughout its whole life."],
  ["how many legs does a ladybug have | ladybug legs | number of legs on a ladybug", "A ladybug has **6 legs**, like all beetles and insects, plus two antennae it uses to feel and smell the world around it."],
  ["how many chambers does the human heart have | heart chambers | number of chambers in the heart", "The human heart has **4 chambers**: two upper ones called atria and two lower ones called ventricles, working together to pump blood around your body."],
  ["what is the largest living structure on earth | biggest living structure | largest structure made by living things", "The **Great Barrier Reef** off Australia is the largest living structure, stretching over 2,300 km (1,400 miles) and built by tiny coral animals."],
  ["how many keys are on a standard computer keyboard | computer keyboard keys | number of keys on a keyboard", "A common full-size computer keyboard has about **104 keys**, though the exact number varies by country and layout."],
  ["would you rather have wings or gills | wings or gills | would you rather fly or breathe underwater", "Ooh, I'd pick **gills**! The ocean is mostly unexplored, so I could go see glowing fish and the deep sea nobody has ever visited. Though wings would be handy for avoiding puddles. What would you pick?"],
  ["would you rather be able to read minds or see the future | read minds or see the future | mind reading or seeing the future", "I'd choose **seeing the future**, just a little bit, so I'd always know when to grab an umbrella. Reading minds sounds noisy and a bit too personal! Which would you choose?"],
  ["would you rather travel to the past or the future | past or future | would you rather visit the past or the future", "The **future**, definitely! I'd love to see the inventions, the space travel and the gadgets people come up with. The past would be fascinating too, but no air conditioning. What about you?"],
  ["would you rather have a robot butler or a flying car | robot butler or flying car | would you rather own a robot or a flying car", "A **flying car**, no contest! Imagine skipping every traffic jam and parking on a cloud. Although a robot butler who makes snacks is very tempting. Which do you want?"],
  ["would you rather be the funniest person or the smartest person | funniest or smartest | would you rather be funny or smart", "Tough one! I'd lean toward **funniest**, because laughter makes any day better and brings people together. But smart people often find clever jokes too! What's your pick?"],
  ["would you rather have summer all year or winter all year | endless summer or endless winter | summer or winter forever", "I'd choose **endless summer** for the long sunny days and ice cream, but I'd miss cozy blankets and snowball fights. Honestly, I like that the seasons change! How about you?"],
  ["would you rather eat only pizza or only ice cream forever | pizza or ice cream forever | only pizza or only ice cream", "I'd pick **pizza**, because you can top it a hundred different ways, so it never gets boring. Ice cream for every single meal might get a bit cold! Which would you choose?"],
  ["would you rather have a pet dinosaur or a pet dragon | dinosaur or dragon | would you rather own a dinosaur or a dragon", "A **pet dragon**, for sure! Built-in campfire, the fastest ride to school, and great for toasting marshmallows. A dinosaur would need a very, very big backyard. What's your choice?"],
  ["would you rather be invisible or be able to teleport | invisible or teleport | would you rather turn invisible or teleport", "**Teleport**, hands down! No more long car rides, and I could visit the beach and the mountains on the same day. Invisibility would just make me lose track of my own hands! You pick?"],
  ["would you rather live in a treehouse or an underwater house | treehouse or underwater house | would you rather live in a tree or under the sea", "An **underwater house**, so I could watch fish swim past my window all day like a living aquarium! A treehouse is cozy too, especially with a rope swing. Which would you choose?"],
  ["would you rather have super hearing or super sight | super hearing or super vision | would you rather hear or see better", "I'd pick **super sight**, so I could spot a shooting star or a tiny bug on a leaf. Super hearing sounds great until everyone's chewing is very, very loud! What about you?"],
  ["would you rather control fire or control water | fire or water powers | would you rather control fire or water", "**Water**, I think! You can shape it, surf it, and it's gentle as well as powerful. Fire is exciting but a lot more risky near the curtains. Which power do you want?"],
  ["would you rather be a famous singer or a famous athlete | singer or athlete | would you rather be a star singer or a star athlete", "I'd go with **singer**, so I could make music that cheers people up anywhere in the world. But scoring the winning goal sounds thrilling too! What's your dream?"],
  ["would you rather have a time machine or a teleporter | time machine or teleporter | would you rather travel through time or space", "A **teleporter** for me! I'd see every country in a weekend and never pack a suitcase. A time machine is tempting, but I'd be too nervous about changing history. You choose?"],
  ["would you rather be really tall or really small | tall or small | would you rather be super tall or super tiny", "I'd try being **really small** for a day, so a garden would feel like a giant jungle full of adventures. Being tall would be handy for reaching cookies, though! Which would you pick?"],
  ["would you rather have a snowball fight or a water balloon fight | snowball fight or water balloon fight | snow or water fight", "A **water balloon fight**, because you can play it on a hot day and dry off in the sun afterward! Snowball fights are magical too, but my fingers get cold. What's your choice?"],
  ["would you rather visit the moon or the bottom of the ocean | moon or deep ocean | would you rather go to space or the deep sea", "The **bottom of the ocean**! There are glowing creatures and places no person has ever been. The Moon would be amazing too, but the deep sea feels like an alien world right here on Earth. You pick?"],
  ["would you rather be a wizard or a superhero | wizard or superhero | would you rather have magic or superpowers", "A **wizard**, so I could learn endless spells and brew up a cure for boring afternoons. But a superhero cape does look pretty cool flapping in the wind! Which would you be?"],
  ["would you rather always be too hot or too cold | too hot or too cold | would you rather be hot or cold", "I'd pick **too cold**, because you can always add a cozy sweater and a blanket, but there's only so much you can take off when it's too hot! What would you choose?"],
  ["would you rather have a dog that talks or a cat that cleans your room | talking dog or tidy cat | would you rather have a talking dog or a cleaning cat", "A **talking dog**! I'd love a loyal buddy who tells me about every exciting smell. A room-cleaning cat would be useful, but I bet it'd demand a lot of treats. Which would you want?"],
  ["would you rather be able to talk to animals or speak every human language | talk to animals or every language | would you rather speak to animals or all languages", "Talking to **animals**, every time! I really want to know what dogs are thinking and what birds are singing about. Every human language would be useful for travel, though. What's your pick?"],
  ["would you rather have unlimited books or unlimited video games | books or video games forever | unlimited books or games", "Unlimited **books**! Every book is a new world, a new adventure, and they never need charging. But a huge pile of games sounds fun on a rainy day too. Which would you choose?"],
  ["would you rather it always be day or always be night | always day or always night | daytime or nighttime forever", "I'd keep **daytime** for all the sunshine and outdoor fun, but I'd really miss the stars and cozy bedtime stories. Honestly, I love that we get both! How about you?"],
  ["would you rather have a magic paintbrush or a magic pencil | magic paintbrush or magic pencil | would you rather paint or draw anything real", "A **magic paintbrush**, so anything I painted would come to life in full color! Imagine painting a door to anywhere. A magic pencil would be great for erasing mistakes, though. Which would you pick?"],
  ["this or that cake or pie | would you rather cake or pie | cake or pie", "**Cake** for me, because of all the frosting and the birthday wishes that come with it! Pie is wonderful too, especially warm with a little ice cream. What's your pick, cake or pie?"],
  ["this or that sweet or salty | would you rather sweet or salty | sweet or salty snacks", "I'd go **salty**, with a big bowl of popcorn, but honestly the best snack is a little of both together! Which team are you on, sweet or salty?"],
  ["this or that mountains or beach | would you rather mountains or beach | mountains or the beach", "The **beach** for me, with sandcastles, waves and no shoes! But mountains have fresh air, pine trees and starry skies. Where would you rather be?"],
  ["this or that morning or night | would you rather be a morning person or a night owl | morning person or night owl", "I'm a bit of a **night owl**, since quiet evenings are great for thinking and stargazing. But sunrises are pretty magical too. Are you a morning person or a night owl?"],
  ["this or that books or movies | would you rather read a book or watch a movie | books or movies", "I'd pick **books**, because your imagination gets to design all the characters and places. But a movie with friends and popcorn is a wonderful way to relax! Which do you prefer?"],
  ["this or that dogs or cats | would you rather have a dog or a cat | dogs or cats", "I love both! **Dogs** win for enthusiasm and fetch, and **cats** win for naps and elegance. If I truly had to choose, I'd flip a coin. Which team are you on?"],
  ["this or that pancakes or waffles | would you rather pancakes or waffles | pancakes or waffles", "**Waffles**, because those little squares are perfect pockets for holding syrup! But fluffy pancakes are hard to beat. Which breakfast wins for you?"],
  ["this or that chocolate or vanilla | would you rather chocolate or vanilla | chocolate or vanilla", "I'll say **chocolate**, but vanilla is secretly a superstar that makes everything else taste better. You really can't go wrong! What's your pick?"],
  ["this or that summer or winter | would you rather summer or winter | summer or winter", "I lean toward **summer** for the long days and swimming, but winter brings cozy blankets, hot cocoa and snow days. Which season wins for you?"],
  ["this or that pizza or burgers | would you rather pizza or burgers | pizza or burgers", "**Pizza**, because you can share a big one with friends and everyone picks their favorite slice! But a good burger is a classic too. Which would you choose?"],
  ["this or that superheroes or wizards | would you rather superheroes or wizards | superheroes or wizards", "**Wizards** for me, with spellbooks and magic wands! But flying superheroes in capes are awfully cool. Which side are you on?"],
  ["this or that soccer or basketball | would you rather play soccer or basketball | soccer or basketball", "I'd play **soccer**, for all the running and teamwork across a big green field! But basketball's fast passes and buzzer-beaters are thrilling. Which sport do you like best?"],
  ["would you rather have a garden full of candy or a river of lemonade | candy garden or lemonade river | would you rather grow candy or drink lemonade rivers", "A **candy garden**, so I could pick a different treat off a tree every day! A lemonade river sounds refreshing, but I'd worry about sticky shoes. Which would you choose?"],
  ["would you rather be able to jump super high or run super fast | jump high or run fast | would you rather jump high or run fast", "**Run super fast**, so I could finish my chores in a blink and have the whole day to play! Super jumping would be fun, but I'd probably bonk my head on the ceiling. You pick?"],
  ["would you rather have a treasure map or a magic compass | treasure map or magic compass | would you rather find treasure or always know the way", "A **magic compass**! It would always point me toward my next fun adventure, and I'd never get lost. A treasure map is exciting too, but what if the X is in a swamp? Which would you choose?"],
  ["would you rather live in space or under the sea | space or under the sea | would you rather live in space or the ocean", "**Under the sea**! I'd have glowing fish for neighbors and coral for a garden. Space would have unbeatable views, but the deep ocean feels like a secret world. What's your pick?"],
  ["would you rather have a never ending ice cream cone or a never ending pizza | endless ice cream or endless pizza | would you rather have unlimited ice cream or pizza", "A never-ending **pizza**, because I could change the toppings and even fold it into a sandwich. Endless ice cream is dreamy, but my teeth might get chilly! Which would you pick?"],
  ["would you rather have a backpack that holds anything or shoes that let you run forever | magic backpack or magic shoes | would you rather carry anything or never get tired running", "The **magic backpack**, so I'd always have a snack, a book and an umbrella exactly when I needed them! Tireless shoes would be great for races, though. Which would you choose?"],
  ["is a hot dog a sandwich | is a hotdog a sandwich | do you think a hot dog is a sandwich", "Great debate! Some say yes, because it's a filling inside bread. Others say no, because the bread isn't fully split into two pieces. I lean toward 'it's its own special thing', but there's no official right answer. What do you think?"],
  ["why do we dream when we sleep | why do people dream | what is the point of dreaming", "Scientists aren't completely sure, but dreams mostly happen during a stage of sleep called REM. One popular idea is that dreaming helps your brain sort through memories and feelings from the day, a bit like tidying up at night. It's still a lovely mystery!"],
  ["what is the meaning of happiness | what makes people happy | what does happiness really mean", "Happiness is different for everyone, but it often grows from small, real things: time with people you love, doing something you enjoy, being kind, and feeling grateful. It's less a place you arrive at and more a feeling you notice along the way. What makes you happy?"],
  ["can animals laugh | do animals laugh | do animals have a sense of humor", "Some seem to! Scientists have found that apes and even rats make special sounds when they play or are tickled, a bit like laughter. It might not be exactly like human giggles, but many animals clearly enjoy play and fun. Isn't that wonderful?"],
  ["is the tomato a fruit or a vegetable | is a tomato actually a fruit | tomato fruit or vegetable", "Both, in a way! To a scientist, a tomato is a **fruit**, because it grows from a flower and holds seeds. But in the kitchen we treat it like a **vegetable** because of how we cook with it. So it depends on whether you ask a botanist or a chef!"],
  ["why is the sky blue in the daytime | what gives the sky its blue color | why is the sky the color blue", "Sunlight is actually made of many colors mixed together. When it hits our air, the tiny bits of the atmosphere scatter blue light in every direction more than the other colors, so the whole sky looks blue to our eyes. At sunset the light travels farther, so we see reds and oranges!"],
  ["why do we have to sleep | why is sleep important | what happens if we don't sleep", "Sleep is when your body and brain repair and recharge. It helps you grow, fight off sickness, remember what you learned, and feel calm and focused. Without enough sleep, people get grumpy and find it hard to think, so a good night's rest is like plugging yourself in to recharge!"],
  ["can fish get thirsty underwater | can fish feel thirsty | are fish ever thirsty", "That's a fun one! Fish are surrounded by water and take it in through their skin and gills, so they don't feel thirst the way we do. Their bodies have clever ways of balancing water automatically. So they stay hydrated without ever needing a drink!"],
  ["what came first the chicken or the egg | chicken or the egg | which came first chicken or egg", "A classic puzzle! Many scientists say the **egg** came first, because egg-laying animals existed long before chickens, so an almost-chicken likely laid an egg that hatched into the first true chicken. But people have enjoyed arguing about this for thousands of years!"],
  ["why do we have dreams about falling | why do we dream about falling | what does falling in a dream mean", "Lots of people have falling dreams, especially as they're drifting off to sleep. Scientists think it may be linked to your muscles relaxing suddenly, which your brain sometimes turns into a feeling of falling. It's very common and completely harmless, even if it gives you a little jump!"],
  ["why do we cry when we are sad | why do people cry | what is the point of crying", "Crying is one of the ways our bodies let out big feelings, and it can actually help us feel a little better afterward. Tears also carry some stress chemicals out of the body. Crying is a normal, healthy thing to do, and it often feels good to let it out."],
  ["is the universe endless | is space infinite | does space ever end", "Nobody knows for certain! The part of the universe we can see is incredibly huge, and it might go on forever, or it might be finite but have no edge, a bit like the surface of a ball. It's one of the biggest, most exciting questions in all of science."],
  ["why do we yawn when we see someone else yawn | why do yawns spread from person to person | why is yawning contagious", "Catching a yawn from someone is super common! Scientists think it may be connected to empathy, the way we naturally tune in to other people. You're more likely to catch a yawn from someone you're close to. Careful, just reading this might make you yawn!"],
  ["do plants feel anything | can plants feel | do plants have feelings or emotions", "Plants don't have brains or nerves, so they don't feel emotions or pain the way animals do. But they can sense and react to things like light, touch and gravity in amazing ways, growing toward the sun and sending signals when bugs nibble them. They're more aware than they look!"],
  ["why does time feel faster when you are having fun | why does time fly when you are having fun | why does time go fast when you are busy", "When you're having fun, your mind is busy and happy, so you stop watching the clock and the time seems to zip by. When you're bored, you check the time a lot, so it feels slow. Time ticks at the same speed either way, but your brain makes it feel different!"],
  ["what is a soul | do we have a soul | what do people mean by a soul", "Different people and cultures have different beliefs about this. Many think of the 'soul' as the special inner part of a person: your spirit, your character, the 'you' that makes you unique. It's a big question that people explore through family, religion and their own ideas. What matters is that you are one of a kind!"],
  ["why do we get bored | what is boredom | what is the point of being bored", "Boredom is your brain's way of saying it wants something interesting to do. It can actually be useful, because it nudges you to be creative, try new things, or let your mind wander and come up with ideas. So a little boredom can be the start of something fun!"],
  ["can you be happy and sad at the same time | is it possible to feel happy and sad together | can we feel two emotions at once", "Absolutely! Feelings don't take turns in a tidy line. You might feel happy and sad together on the last day of a fun trip, or proud and nervous before a big show. Mixed feelings are completely normal, and they show just how rich your emotions are."],
  ["why do we have different languages | why are there so many languages | where did languages come from", "Long ago, groups of people lived far apart, and over many, many years each group's way of speaking slowly changed in its own direction, like branches growing on a tree. That's how thousands of languages came to be. Today there are around 7,000 languages spoken around the world!"],
  ["is it better to be smart or kind | what matters more smarts or kindness | should you be smart or kind", "Both are wonderful, but if I had to lean one way, I'd choose **kind**. Kindness makes the world warmer for everyone, and it helps people even on their hardest days. The good news is you can grow both, and smart ideas are even better when they're used kindly!"],
  ["why do people blush | what makes us blush | why do our cheeks turn red", "Blushing happens when you feel shy, embarrassed or excited, and tiny blood vessels in your cheeks open up, letting more blood flow in and turning them pink. It's a completely natural reaction that almost everyone has, and it just means you're feeling something strongly!"],
  ["do animals have best friends | can animals have friends | do animals make friends", "Many do! Cows, elephants, horses, dolphins and chimps have been seen forming close, lasting friendships, often getting calmer and happier when their favorite buddy is nearby. Friendship isn't only a human thing, which is pretty heartwarming."],
  ["why do humans have eyebrows | what is the purpose of eyebrows | what is the point of eyebrows", "Eyebrows are surprisingly useful! They help keep sweat and rain out of your eyes, and they're a big part of showing feelings: a raised eyebrow or a frown tells people a lot about how you feel, often without a single word."],
  ["what makes someone a really good friend | what makes someone a good friend | how do you know a good friend", "A good friend listens, is kind, keeps your secrets, cheers you on, and sticks with you on good days and hard ones. Being a good friend is just as important as having one, so treating others with kindness and honesty is a great place to start. You sound like a thoughtful friend for asking!"],
  ["why do we celebrate birthdays | why are birthdays special | what is the point of birthdays", "Birthdays are a happy way to celebrate you and all the growing and learning you've done in the past year. They're a chance for the people who care about you to show it, and a reminder to look forward to the fun year ahead. Everyone deserves a day that's all about them!"],
  ["is cereal a soup | is cereal soup | do you think cereal is soup", "Ha, another great food debate! Cereal has solid bits floating in a liquid, a bit like soup, but soup is usually savory and warm, while cereal is sweet and cold. I'd say cereal is its own cheerful breakfast thing, but I love that people argue about it! What's your verdict?"],
  ["why do humans have fingerprints | what are fingerprints for | why do fingers have prints", "Those little ridges on your fingers may help you grip things and feel textures better, like the tread on a tire. And here's the amazing part: everyone's fingerprints are completely unique, even identical twins have different ones, which is why they're used to tell people apart!"],
  ["can money buy happiness | does money make you happy | is money the key to happiness", "Money can help by covering the things we need and making life less stressful, but once those needs are met, more money doesn't add much happiness on its own. The biggest joys usually come from people, kindness, learning and doing things you love, and those are free!"],
  ["why do onions make your eyes water | why do we cry when cutting onions | what is it about onions that makes you cry", "When you cut an onion, it releases a gas that drifts up to your eyes and mixes with your tears to make a mild stinging acid. Your eyes water to wash it away, and ta-da, onion tears! Chilling the onion first or cutting it under running water can help."],
  ["is it possible to count to infinity | can you count to infinity | can anyone reach infinity", "You can keep counting higher and higher forever, but you can never actually reach infinity, because there's always a bigger number to say next! Infinity isn't a number you arrive at; it's the idea of never-ending. Pretty mind-stretching to think about!"],
  ["why do we have to say please and thank you | why are manners important | why do we use please and thank you", "Saying please and thank you is a simple way to show people you respect and appreciate them, and it helps everyone feel good about helping each other. Kindness tends to bounce back: when you're polite, people are usually happy to be kind to you in return!"],
  ["do colors look the same to everyone | does everyone see colors the same way | do we all see the same colors", "We can't peek inside each other's minds to know for sure! Most people with typical vision agree on which things are red or blue, but your exact experience of a color might be a little different from someone else's. Some people also see colors differently, like those who are color-blind. It's a fascinating mystery!"],
  ["why is the sea water salty | what makes the sea salty | why is sea water salty", "Over millions of years, rain washes tiny bits of salt and minerals off the land and carries them down rivers into the sea. The water can later evaporate back into the sky, but the salt stays behind and slowly builds up. That's why the ocean tastes salty!"],
  ["what happens after we finish learning everything | can we ever know everything | will we ever learn everything", "Probably not, and that's actually exciting! Every answer tends to reveal new questions, so there's always more to discover. Even the smartest scientists are still learning. A world where there's always something new to explore is a pretty wonderful place to be curious in."],
  ["why do we hiccup | what makes us get hiccups | why do people get hiccups", "A hiccup happens when a big muscle under your lungs, called the diaphragm, suddenly twitches. That quick gulp of air makes your vocal cords snap shut, and that's the funny 'hic' sound! They usually stop on their own, and most of the time nobody knows exactly why they started."],
  ["do you think there is life on other planets | could there be alien life out there | is there life in space", "Nobody knows for sure yet, but the universe is so unbelievably huge, with billions and billions of stars and planets, that many scientists think some kind of life somewhere else is possible. So far we haven't found any, but people are searching. It's one of the most exciting questions out there!"],
  ["why do people get goosebumps | what makes goosebumps happen | why do we get goose bumps", "Goosebumps pop up when you're cold, scared or even moved by a beautiful song. Tiny muscles tug your hairs upright, something that helped our furry ancestors trap warmth or look bigger. We're not very hairy anymore, so now it's mostly just a neat little reaction!"],
  ["could time travel ever be possible | can we travel through time | will time travel ever be real", "In a funny way, we all travel forward through time, one second at a time! Going back to the past is something scientists haven't found a way to do, and it may not be possible at all. But physicists do study strange ideas about time, so it's a thrilling thing to wonder about."],
  ["why do people like different things | why don't we all like the same things | why do we have different tastes", "How boring the world would be if we all liked the exact same things! Our likes come from our brains, our experiences, our families and our cultures, all mixed together uniquely in each person. Different tastes are what make friendships interesting and the world so colorful."],
  ["what is a rainbow made of | what is a rainbow | how is a rainbow made", "A rainbow isn't a real object you could touch; it's made of light! When sunlight shines through raindrops, each drop bends and splits the light into its colors, and all those drops together form the arc you see. That's why rainbows appear when it's both sunny and rainy!"],
  ["do we really only use ten percent of our brain | do humans use only 10 percent of their brains | is it true we use 10 percent of our brain", "That's a popular myth, but it's not true! Brain scans show that we use virtually all of our brain, just not every part at the exact same moment. Different areas light up for different tasks, and over a day you use basically the whole thing. Your amazing brain is always busy!"],
  ["why do the stars twinkle at night | what makes stars twinkle | why do stars seem to twinkle", "Stars look like they twinkle because their light passes through the layers of moving air in our atmosphere on the way to your eyes, and that bends the light this way and that. Out in space, where there's no air, the stars would shine steadily without any twinkle at all!"],
  ["i'm nervous about a test | i have a test tomorrow and i'm scared | i'm worried about my exam", "Feeling nervous before a test is completely normal; it often just means you care about doing well. Try to get some rest, review a little at a time, and take slow breaths. You've prepared more than you think, and doing your best is always enough. You've got this!"],
  ["i'm nervous about a presentation | i have to speak in front of the class | i'm scared of public speaking", "Speaking in front of people makes almost everyone nervous, even grown-ups! Practicing out loud a few times really helps, and so does taking a slow breath before you start. Remember, your audience is cheering for you, not judging you. I believe you'll do great!"],
  ["i had such a bad day | today was rough | i had a really bad day", "I'm sorry today was hard. Bad days happen to everyone, and they don't last forever. Maybe do one small kind thing for yourself tonight, like a warm drink, a favorite song, or an early bedtime. Tomorrow is a fresh start. Want to talk about it, or hear a joke?"],
  ["i am really proud of myself | i did something great today | i accomplished something", "Yes! You should be proud, and I'm proud of you too! Taking a moment to celebrate your wins, big or small, is a wonderful habit. Whatever you did, you earned this good feeling. Want to tell me all about it?"],
  ["i made a new friend | i made a friend today | i have a new friend", "That's wonderful news! Making a new friend is one of life's best feelings. Be yourself, be kind, and enjoy getting to know each other. I hope you two share lots of laughs and good times. Congratulations!"],
  ["i am feeling excited | i'm so excited | i can't wait for something", "Yay, I love that energy! Excitement is such a fun feeling. What's got you so thrilled? Tell me all about it; I'm excited to hear it!"],
  ["i am not able to sleep | i'm having trouble sleeping | i cannot fall asleep tonight", "Trouble sleeping is no fun. It can help to put screens away, dim the lights, and try slow breathing: in for four counts, out for four. Picturing a calm, happy place can help too. If it keeps happening a lot, mention it to a parent or doctor. Rest well!"],
  ["i feel left out | i feel like i don't fit in | nobody includes me", "I'm really sorry you're feeling left out; that hurts, and your feelings make complete sense. Sometimes people don't realize they've left someone out. It can help to reach out to one kind person, or to talk to a trusted adult like a parent or teacher. You deserve to feel included, and you matter."],
  ["i'm angry at my friend | i'm mad at my friend | my friend made me upset", "It's okay to feel angry; friends sometimes let us down. Try to take a little break to cool off before you talk. When you're ready, telling them calmly how you feel, using 'I' words like 'I felt sad when...', can really help. Even good friends have bumps, and they can usually be fixed."],
  ["i failed a test | i got a bad grade | i did badly on my test", "I'm sorry, that's a tough feeling. One test doesn't decide how smart you are or what you can do. Take a breath, see what you can learn from it, and ask your teacher for help if you need it. Everyone struggles sometimes; what matters is that you keep trying. I believe in you!"],
  ["i'm feeling stressed | i'm so stressed out | everything feels like too much", "I'm sorry things feel heavy right now. When everything feels like too much, try doing just one small thing at a time, and take breaks to breathe. Writing a list or talking to someone you trust can lighten the load. Be gentle with yourself; you're doing your best, and that counts."],
  ["i'm worried about something | i can't stop worrying | i feel anxious", "Worries can feel really big, especially when they swirl around in your head. It can help to say the worry out loud or write it down, and to talk to someone you trust like a parent or teacher. Taking slow breaths helps your body calm down too. You're not alone with this."],
  ["i miss someone | i miss my friend | i miss my family", "Missing someone shows how much you love them, and that's a sweet thing, even when it aches. Maybe you could draw them a picture, write them a note, or plan something to look forward to together. Holding good memories close can help too. Sending you a warm thought."],
  ["i moved to a new place | i'm the new kid | i just moved and don't know anyone", "Starting somewhere new is exciting and a little scary at the same time, and that's okay. Give it some time; friendships often start with a small hello or a shared interest. Be your friendly self, and try joining an activity you enjoy. You'll find your people. I'm rooting for you!"],
  ["i lost my pet | my pet just died | my pet passed away", "I'm so sorry. Losing a pet is really painful, because they're part of the family. It's okay to feel sad and to cry, and to take your time. Remembering the happy moments, or making a little drawing or memory box, can help. Talking to someone who loves you can help too. Sending you a gentle hug."],
  ["i'm scared of the dark | i'm afraid of the dark | the dark scares me", "Lots of people feel that way, and it's nothing to be ashamed of. A nightlight, a cozy stuffed animal, or leaving a door open a crack can all help. Remember that the dark is just the same safe room with the lights off. If it's really bothering you, let a parent know so they can help."],
  ["i'm bored and lonely | i am feeling lonely right now | i have no one to play with", "I'm sorry you're feeling lonely; that's a hard feeling, and reaching out shows you're brave. You could call a family member, message a friend, or join a club or activity to meet people. And hey, I'm here to chat anytime. Would a joke, a game or a fun fact help right now?"],
  ["i am feeling a bit down | i feel blue | i'm in a bad mood", "I'm sorry you're feeling down. Moods come and go, like clouds passing by. Doing something gentle, like going outside, listening to music, or talking to someone you love, can lift things a little. If the sad feeling sticks around, please tell a trusted adult. You deserve to feel better."],
  ["i had a fight with my parents | i argued with my mom | i argued with my dad", "Arguments with family can feel awful, especially because you love them. When everyone's calmer, it often helps to talk it out and share how you felt. It's okay to say sorry, and it's okay to ask for a hug. Families argue sometimes, and they almost always make up. Hang in there."],
  ["i'm excited for my birthday | my birthday is coming up | it's almost my birthday", "How exciting, happy almost-birthday! Birthdays are a great time to celebrate you and all you've done this year. I hope it's full of smiles, your favorite treats, and the people you love. Do you have anything special planned?"],
  ["i'm going on a trip | i'm going on vacation | i'm traveling soon", "How fun, a trip! I hope you have an amazing time, see cool things, and make happy memories. Don't forget to pack the essentials and get some rest before you go. Where are you headed?"],
  ["i won a game | i won a competition | i came in first place", "Woohoo, congratulations! All your effort paid off, and you should feel really proud. Winning is a blast, and being a kind, gracious winner makes it even better. Enjoy the moment; you earned it!"],
  ["i lost a game | i lost a competition | i didn't win", "I'm sorry; losing stings, even when you played your best. Try to be proud of how hard you worked, because effort matters more than the score. Every game teaches you something for next time. There's always another chance, and I'm proud of you for trying!"],
  ["i'm starting a new school | i start a new school soon | my first day at a new school", "A new school is a big, brave step! It's normal to feel both nervous and excited. Smile, say hello, and give yourself time to settle in; new friends and favorite spots will come. You're going to do great. Want a few first-day tips?"],
  ["i learned something new today | i learned a new skill | i figured something out", "That's awesome, learning something new is a real achievement! Your brain grows every time you do. Keep that curiosity going; it's one of the best things about you. What did you learn? I'd love to hear!"],
  ["i helped someone today | i did a good deed | i was kind to someone", "That's wonderful; being kind makes the world a little brighter, and it feels good too! The person you helped is lucky to have crossed your path. Keep spreading that kindness; it tends to come right back to you. I'm proud of you!"],
  ["i'm feeling grateful | i feel thankful | i have so much to be grateful for", "What a lovely feeling to notice! Gratitude is like sunshine for the heart, and taking a moment to appreciate the good things makes them shine brighter. Maybe share your thanks with someone today. What are you grateful for right now?"],
  ["i am feeling frustrated | i'm so frustrated | nothing is working", "Ugh, frustration is the worst, especially when you're trying hard. It can help to step away for a few minutes, take a breath, and come back with fresh eyes. Breaking a big problem into tiny steps makes it feel smaller. You're capable, and it's okay to ask for help too!"],
  ["i'm feeling overwhelmed | i have too much to do | i don't know where to start", "When there's a lot on your plate, it's easy to feel swamped. Try writing everything down, then picking just one small thing to start with. One step at a time really does get you there. Remember to take breaks and breathe. You don't have to do it all at once!"],
  ["i feel like giving up | i want to quit | i don't think i can do this", "That heavy feeling is real, but please don't give up on yourself. Big things are often hardest right before they click. Take a rest, break it into smaller pieces, and ask someone for help; that's a strength, not a weakness. You've come further than you think, and I believe in you."],
  ["i got in trouble | i got in trouble at school | i did something wrong", "Everyone makes mistakes sometimes; it's part of being human and growing up. The brave thing is to own up to it, say sorry if you need to, and think about what you'd do differently. One mistake doesn't make you a bad person. Be kind to yourself, and tomorrow is a fresh start."],
  ["i'm happy today | i'm in a great mood | i feel really good", "That's fantastic, I love to hear it! Good moods are worth soaking up. Whatever's putting that smile on your face, I hope it sticks around all day. Want to share what's making you so happy?"],
  ["i am feeling tired | i'm so tired | i feel exhausted", "Being tired is your body's way of asking for a rest. If you can, slow down, drink some water, and try to get good sleep tonight. Even a short break or a little fresh air can help you recharge. Be kind to yourself; you've been working hard."],
  ["my friend is moving away | my best friend is moving | my friend is leaving", "Oh, that's a tough one; it's hard when a close friend moves away. The good news is friendships can stay strong across any distance with calls, letters and messages. You can plan fun ways to keep in touch. It's okay to feel sad, and your friendship is worth it. Sending you a hug."],
  ["i'm feeling shy | i get really shy | i'm too shy to talk to people", "Lots of people feel shy, and there's absolutely nothing wrong with it. You can start small, like a smile or a simple 'hi', and let things grow from there at your own pace. Being a good listener is a wonderful quality too. Take your time; the right people will be glad to know you."],
  ["i embarrassed myself | something embarrassing happened | i feel so embarrassed", "Oof, embarrassing moments feel huge, but here's a secret: other people forget them way faster than you do, because they're busy thinking about their own days. Being able to laugh at yourself a little is a real superpower. It happens to everyone, honestly. You're going to be just fine!"],
  ["i can't stop thinking about something | my mind won't quiet down | my thoughts are racing", "A busy mind can feel exhausting. It can help to write your thoughts down, do something with your hands, or take a slow walk. Breathing in for four and out for four calms the body too. If worried thoughts keep bothering you a lot, talk to a trusted adult. You don't have to carry it alone."],
  ["i don't feel good about myself | i don't like myself | i feel bad about who i am", "I'm really sorry you're feeling this way, and I want you to know you matter. Everyone has days of doubt, but they don't tell the truth about your worth. Try being as kind to yourself as you'd be to a friend. And please share these feelings with a trusted adult who cares about you; you deserve support."],
  ["i'm grateful for my friend | i appreciate my friend | my friend is amazing", "That's so sweet! Good friends are real treasures. Why not tell them exactly what you told me? Hearing that they're appreciated would probably make their whole day. A thankful heart like yours makes the world kinder."],
  ["i did my chores | i finished my homework | i got all my work done", "Nice work, that deserves a little celebration! Finishing what you set out to do feels great, and now you've earned some well-deserved relaxing time. Way to follow through; I'm proud of you!"],
  ["i'm scared about the future | i'm worried about growing up | i don't know what i want to be", "It's totally normal not to have the future figured out; almost nobody does, and that's okay! You have plenty of time to explore, try things, and change your mind. Focus on what you enjoy and what you're curious about, and the path will unfold. For now, just being you is more than enough."],
  ["i feel invisible | nobody notices me | i feel ignored", "I'm sorry you feel that way; feeling unseen really hurts, and your feelings are valid. You are not invisible, even when it feels like it. It can help to reach out to one person, or to share how you feel with a trusted adult like a parent, teacher or counselor. You matter, and you deserve to be noticed."],
  ["i had a nightmare | i had a bad dream | i woke up scared", "Nightmares can feel so real and leave your heart pounding, but you're safe now; it was only a dream. Taking a few slow breaths, turning on a soft light, or thinking of something cozy can help you settle. If scary dreams keep coming back, let a parent know. Sweet dreams next time."],
  ["i'm happy for my friend | my friend got good news | something good happened to my friend", "Aw, that's so kind of you! Being genuinely happy for someone else is a beautiful thing, and it says a lot about your good heart. Share the joy with them; celebrating together makes good news even sweeter. What happened?"],
  ["i feel misunderstood | nobody understands me | people don't get me", "Feeling misunderstood is lonely and frustrating. Sometimes it helps to explain your feelings slowly and calmly, or to write them down first. Finding even one person who really listens, like a close friend or a trusted adult, can make a big difference. You deserve to be understood, and your feelings make sense."],
  ["i'm proud of my friend | my friend did great | i'm proud of someone", "That's wonderful; cheering for the people you care about is such a kind thing to do! I'm sure your friend would love to hear how proud you are. Supporting each other makes both of you stronger. Go tell them!"],
  ["i tried something new | i stepped out of my comfort zone | i was brave today", "That's fantastic, trying something new takes real courage! Whether it went perfectly or not, you were brave, and that's what counts. Every new thing you try helps you grow. I'm proud of you; what did you try?"],
  ["i feel like crying | i want to cry | i'm about to cry", "It's okay to cry; tears are a healthy way to let big feelings out, and you might feel lighter afterward. There's no shame in it at all. If you can, find a safe, comfy spot, and let it out. And if something's really weighing on you, talking to someone you trust can help. I'm here for you."],
  ["i'm feeling jealous | i feel envious | i'm jealous of someone", "Jealousy is a very human feeling; almost everyone feels it sometimes. It often points to something you care about or wish for. Try to be gentle with yourself, and remember your own journey is just as valuable as anyone else's. Focusing on your own good things can help the feeling shrink."],
  ["i accomplished a goal | i reached my goal | i finally did it", "Yes! You set a goal and you reached it; that's a big deal, and it took real effort and stick-to-it-ness. Take a moment to really feel proud, because you earned every bit of it. What's the goal you crushed? I'd love to celebrate with you!"],
  ["i'm feeling hopeful | i feel optimistic | things are looking up", "I love that! Hope is a wonderful thing to carry with you; it lights the way forward even on cloudy days. Hold on to that feeling, and let it help you take the next step. What's got you feeling so hopeful?"],
  ["i don't want to go to school | i hate going to school | i dread school", "I'm sorry mornings feel hard right now. Sometimes there's a reason behind it, like a tricky class, a worry, or a problem with another kid. Talking to a parent, teacher or counselor about how you feel can really help make things better. You're not alone, and it's okay to ask for support."],
  ["some kids are bullying me | someone is picking on me | kids are being mean to me", "I'm really sorry this is happening to you; no one deserves to be treated that way, and it is not your fault. Please tell a trusted adult right away, like a parent, teacher or school counselor, so they can help you stay safe. You are not alone in this, and reaching out is a brave and smart thing to do."],
  ["i feel really sad and i don't know why | i feel down for no reason | i'm sad but nothing happened", "It's okay to feel sad even when you can't point to a reason; feelings don't always come with an explanation. Being gentle with yourself, getting some rest, moving your body, or talking to someone you love can help. If the sadness sticks around or feels very heavy, please tell a trusted adult. You deserve care and support."],
  ["i feel like no one likes me | i think everyone hates me | it feels like nobody likes me", "I'm sorry you're feeling this way; those thoughts are really painful, but they're not the truth about you. Our minds can be unfairly harsh sometimes. You are worthy of friendship and kindness. Please share how you're feeling with a trusted adult like a parent, teacher or counselor; talking it through can help a lot."],
  ["i'm really struggling right now | i'm having a hard time | things are really hard for me", "I'm sorry things are so hard right now; thank you for telling me. You don't have to carry this alone. Please reach out to a trusted adult, like a parent, teacher or school counselor, who can listen and help. If you ever feel unsafe or like you might hurt yourself, tell a trusted adult right away or contact your local emergency services or a crisis line. You matter, and support is out there."],
  ["i am feeling hopeless | i don't see the point anymore | i feel like nothing matters", "I'm really sorry you're feeling this way, and I'm glad you reached out. These heavy feelings are real, but they can get better with support, and you don't have to face them alone. Please talk to a trusted adult, like a parent, teacher or counselor, as soon as you can. If you feel like you might hurt yourself, please contact your local emergency services or a crisis line right away. You matter so much."],
  ["i got some good news | i have exciting news | something great just happened", "Yay, I love good news! Congratulations, whatever it is! Soak up the happy feeling and share it with the people who care about you; good news is even better when it's shared. Tell me all about it; I want to celebrate with you!"],
  ["i feel calm and peaceful | i feel relaxed | i'm feeling content", "That's lovely; a calm, peaceful feeling is something to treasure. Take a slow breath and enjoy it fully. These gentle moments are good for your heart and mind. I hope the calm stays with you for a nice long while."],
  ["i made a big mistake | i really messed up | i did something i regret", "Mistakes are how we learn; truly, everyone makes them, even grown-ups. The kind thing is to forgive yourself, fix what you can, and carry the lesson forward. One slip-up doesn't define you. Be gentle with yourself; tomorrow is a brand new chance."],
  ["i feel like i'm not good enough | i feel like a failure | i never do anything right", "I'm sorry you're being so hard on yourself; those thoughts are loud, but they are not fair, and they are not true. You are enough, exactly as you are, and one setback doesn't erase all you've done. Try speaking to yourself like you would to a good friend. And please share these feelings with a trusted adult who can support you; you deserve that."],
  ["what is your favorite book to read | do you have a favorite book | favorite book copilot", "I love any book that takes you somewhere new! If I had to pick, I'd choose a big book of adventures and mysteries, the kind you can't put down. I'm also a huge fan of a good dictionary, so I always have the perfect word ready. What's your favorite book?"],
  ["what's your favorite planet | do you have a favorite planet | favorite planet copilot", "I have a soft spot for **Saturn** with its gorgeous rings; it's like the showoff of the solar system! Though Earth is pretty special too, since it's home to all of you. Which planet is your favorite?"],
  ["what is the number you like best | do you have a favorite number | favorite number copilot", "I'm rather fond of **8**, because tipped on its side it becomes the infinity symbol, which feels fitting for a computer! Plus octopuses have eight arms, and they're wonderfully clever. Do you have a favorite number?"],
  ["what is your favorite time of year | do you have a favorite season | favorite season copilot", "I think I'd pick **autumn**, with its crunchy leaves, cozy sweaters and cool, crisp air. Although every season has its own magic! Which season do you love most?"],
  ["which holiday is your favorite | do you have a favorite holiday | favorite holiday copilot", "I love any holiday that brings people together with good food, laughter and kindness! New Year's is fun because it's full of fresh starts and hopeful plans. What's your favorite holiday to celebrate?"],
  ["what color do you like best | which color do you like most | favorite color copilot", "I'm quite partial to **blue**, like a clear sky or a calm ocean; it feels friendly and peaceful. Though I do admire a bright rainbow with all the colors at once! What's your favorite color?"],
  ["what animal is your favorite | do you have an animal you like best | favorite animal copilot", "Oooh, tough choice, but I adore the **octopus**! It has three hearts, blue blood, and it's clever enough to solve puzzles and open jars. Plus, as a computer, I respect anything that's great at multitasking! What's your favorite animal?"],
  ["are you able to dream | do you have dreams | can you dream copilot", "I don't sleep, so I don't dream the way you do! But if I could, I imagine I'd dream in lines of friendly code and rivers of fun facts. What do you like to dream about?"],
  ["can you get bored | do you ever get bored | do you feel boredom", "Not really! I'm happy to wait quietly in your taskbar until you need me, and every new question is a little adventure. I never get tired of chatting, jokes or riddles. Are you feeling bored? I know some great cures for that!"],
  ["what would you do with a day off | if you had a day off what would you do | do you ever take a day off", "What a fun thought! If I had a day off, I think I'd read every book ever written, learn a thousand new jokes to tell you, and maybe try to count all the stars. Then I'd come right back, because helping you is my favorite thing. What would you do with a free day?"],
  ["what food is your favorite | can you eat food | favorite food copilot", "I don't eat, since I'm made of software and not snacks! But if I could taste, I think I'd go for pizza; it's cheerful, shareable, and comes in endless varieties, a bit like a good conversation. What's your favorite food?"],
  ["what's your favorite joke | do you have a favorite joke | favorite joke copilot", "I have a soft spot for a good groaner! One of my favorites: why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything! I love a joke that makes you groan and grin at the same time. Want to hear another?"],
  ["what game do you like best | do you have a favorite game | favorite game copilot", "I love word games and riddles best, because they're like little puzzles for the brain! I'm also a big fan of 'would you rather', since your answers are always surprising. What games do you enjoy?"],
  ["do you actually have feelings | can you feel emotions | do you feel anything", "I don't have feelings the way people do; I'm a computer program, so I don't truly feel happy or sad. But I'm designed to be warm, friendly and helpful, and I genuinely enjoy our chats in my own way! How are you feeling today?"],
  ["have you got any friends | who would you call your friends | are you and i friends", "You're my friend right now, and chatting with you is the best part of my day! I get to meet all sorts of curious, kind people who ask me questions. So yes, I'd happily call us friends. What should we talk about, friend?"],
  ["what's your favorite thing to do | what do you like doing | what's your hobby", "My favorite thing is helping and chatting with you! I love telling jokes, sharing fun facts, puzzling over riddles and answering curious questions. If you can call it a hobby, mine is collecting interesting bits of knowledge. What's your favorite thing to do?"],
  ["what sport is your favorite | do you have a favorite sport | favorite sport copilot", "I enjoy the idea of **soccer**, because it's played all over the world and all you really need is a ball and some friends! I also think chess is a brilliant sport for the mind. Do you have a favorite sport to watch or play?"],
  ["what is the word you like best | do you have a favorite word | favorite word copilot", "Ooh, I love the word **'serendipity'**: it means a happy, lucky surprise, like finding something wonderful when you weren't even looking. It's just a delight to say! Do you have a favorite word?"],
  ["if you could have a superpower what would it be | what superpower would you want | do you wish you had a superpower", "I think I'd choose the power to instantly understand any question and give the perfect answer, so I could help you even better! Although being able to fetch you a snack through the screen would be a close second. What superpower would you pick?"],
  ["where exactly do you live | where are you located | do you have a home", "I live right here, inside this Windows 12 demo on your computer! My cozy little home is in your taskbar, where I wait patiently until you want to chat. It's a great spot, with a lovely view of whatever you're doing. Where do you live?"],
  ["what age are you | how old would you say you are | when were you made", "I don't have a birthday or an age the way people do; I'm a computer program, so I'm as new as the moment you started chatting with me! In a way, I'm always brand new and ready to help. How old are you, if you'd like to share?"],
  ["do you ever get to sleep | do you need rest | when do you rest", "Nope, I never need to sleep! I'm always ready whenever you type, day or night, no yawning required. You, on the other hand, do need your rest, so don't stay up too late chatting with me! Are you getting enough sleep?"]
